@startuml needsblock_height_bound
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' needsblock_height_bound — the needs-a-block card's height, in three acts.
' Converted from Mermaid in the v26.8 audit (never rendered until now).
'
' Read it left to right as a debugging story, because that is what it is: a
' bug, a fix that created a second bug, and the fix that finally located the
' decision in the right object. The transferable lesson is in the two dashed
' arrows at the bottom — a sizeHint is a SUGGESTION and a stretch factor is a
' CLAIM, and confusing the two is why act two looked right and rendered wrong.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title The needs-a-block card's height — bug, over-correction, and the real fix

package "v21 — unbounded" {
  component "20 due tasks" as b1
  component "rows in a QVBoxLayout" as b2
  component "layout minimum =\nSUM of children" as b3
  component "QMainWindow minimum grows" as b4
  component "<b>window cannot shrink</b>" as b5
  b1 --> b2
  b2 --> b3
  b3 --> b4
  b4 --> b5
}

package "v22 — self-capped (wrong)" {
  component "QScrollArea, max 280px" as c1
  component "window free again ✓" as c2
  component "but sizeHint is a\nCACHED GUESS" as c3
  component "<b>card squashed to 2 lines</b>\nover an empty panel ✗" as c4
  c1 --> c2
  c1 --> c3
  c3 --> c4
}

package "v22.1 — the panel decides" {
  component "GlancePanel::refresh()" as d1
  component "gate closed?" as d2
  component "stretch → card\n(card IS the panel, §E)" as d3
  component "stretch → day content\ncard sizes to its strip" as d4
  component "rows fill the height;\nscroll only when it runs out" as d5
  d1 --> d2
  d2 --> d3 : yes
  d2 --> d4 : no
  d3 --> d5
}

b5 ..> c2 : the scroll area's small constant\nMINIMUM survives into v22.1
c4 ..> d1 : <b>stretch factors CLAIM space;</b>\n<b>hints only suggest it</b>

note bottom of d5
  The fix that stuck moved the decision UP —
  a child widget cannot know whether it deserves
  the room, because that depends on its siblings.
  Only the layout's owner has that view.
end note
@enduml
